    author_source: detected
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-28T06:02:24.363Z","harness:codex","2026-09-28 skill review: corrected stale claims that unknown local dependency IDs silently pass creation and that reciprocal inverse spellings necessarily create an ordering cycle. Corrected graph impact direction vocabulary and graph plan meaning. Exhaustive snapshots now explicitly bypass budget truncation only into external consumers, while normal loops stay bounded. Added per-query semantic quality and original-versus-recovered release guidance. Generated docs/skills, SDK parity, grammar and completed-task token gates passed before these targeted corrections; linked docs validation is rerun afterward."
  "2026-09-28T07:22:56.183Z","harness:codex","PR 1333 annotation review: added progressive-disclosure guidance for plain-text note/comment inputs, intentional JSON events, and history-preserving --edit corrections. The guidance prevents JSON-encoding a text object into a plain-text argument."
  "2026-10-18T03:09:32.536Z","harness:codex","GitHub intake https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1494 belongs to the canonical open public-surface consistency owner. Full live metadata and verified history were reread. Current source confirms deprecated list-open/list-all spellings remain in the list unknown-field diagnostic and root help examples. Preserve compatibility aliases; follow up with canonical examples and an independently generated alias-refusal guard covering errors and help. This is intake only and no implementation claim is taken while completing the dependency cohort. Full report:\n\n## What happens\n\nOn pm 2026.10.17, the CLI still teaches two deprecated commands in its own guidance, after #1303 fixed the help examples and the generated agent block:\n\n```console\n$ pm list --fields bogus\n...\nexamples:\n  - pm list-open --fields id,title,status,type,updated_at\n  - pm list --fields id,title,parent,priority --limit 10\n  - pm list-all --fields id,title,body --limit 5\n\n$ pm list-all --limit 1\nDeprecated command `list-all`; use `pm list --all`.\n```\n\nAn agent that follows the error's first or third example gets a deprecation warning on the next call, so recovering from one error costs two extra round trips.\n\nSources on `main`:\n- `src/sdk/query/list.ts` (the `unknown_field_projection` error): the `examples` array lists `pm list-open …` and `pm list-all …`.\n- `src/cli/help-content.ts` `ROOT_HELP_BUNDLE.examples`: lists `pm list-open --limit 10`.\n\n## Expected\n\nEvery example in errors, help bundles and generated guidance uses the canonical spelling: `pm list --status open …` and `pm list --all …`. The deprecation alias map in `src/sdk/cli-contracts/command-aliases.ts` already knows both replacements.\n\n## Suggestion\n\nA single guard would stop this class of regression for good. Add a test that collects every string under `examples` (help bundles, error details, guidance templates), parses its argv, and fails when it resolves to a deprecated alias. The existing `guidance-freshness` spec covers the generated block but not error `examples`."
  "2026-10-18T08:35:37.011Z","harness:codex","Active delivery: resolve GH-1494 canonical command examples across help and SDK diagnostic guidance, with a regression guard derived from the alias registry. Bundled with uniform output-format ergonomics. Keep this broader consistency programme open for its other acceptance criteria."
  "2026-10-18T10:21:12.419Z","harness:codex","PR #1498 review follow-up: the initial exact-head checks all passed. Sourcery identified that the current canonical-example regressions cover help narratives and two diagnostic paths but not a single cross-source guard. Actively extending regression coverage across example-bearing source and generated guidance; no production behavior change planned. CodeRabbit full review explicitly requested because automatic review was skipped; Sourcery full review quota and Greptile trial expiry remain unavailable-review limitations."
  "2026-10-18T10:27:39.860Z","harness:codex","Review regression evidence for PR #1498: the new source-wide guard initially failed on deprecated aliases in help literals and package-install diagnostic builders. Runtime help previously normalized many literals; package recovery examples themselves still needed canonical spelling. Canonicalized example sources plus matching retry messages, preserved attempted-command/normalized-argv evidence, and added generated AGENTS/CLAUDE command checks without new production test seams. Focused final run passed all 306 tests in 8 files, including existing contract, setup and extension recovery suites; affected-file ESLint passed. Source changes are command text only. Full static gate and CodeRabbit requested review remain running before push."
  "2026-10-18T10:43:05.782Z","harness:codex","PR #1498 final review follow-up: CodeRabbit full review completed for 404bcfe with no actionable code comments and no inline threads; its docstring warning is addressed with documentation on all six touched undocumented helpers plus the new test helpers. Repository docstring quality and affected-file ESLint passed. All 306 focused tests in 8 files passed again through the actual linked-test runner with trusted local source provenance. Full static prefix passed dependency/security, generated contracts/docs, repository/package boundaries, grammar/refusal/token/MCP audits, tracker context, registry, SDK surface and all ten SDK import budgets. Two final local transport runs failed on a qualified runner: claim best 417ms versus 415ms, then next best 487ms versus 440ms. No further timing retries or ceiling changes. Graph-composition and record-integrity passed separately. Final bounded mutation attempt retained 2 timeouts on unchanged dependency-provenance mutants, 339 killed and 7 approved equivalent survivors; the gate correctly failed. Earlier same-source mutation/coverage proof is retained separately. Final-head hosted static/mutation/coverage checks must pass before merge. Latest npm pm-changelog remains 2026.10.17. Sourcery full-review quota and Greptile trial expiry are unavailable-review limitations, not approvals. Implementation is complete; returning this broader programme to open and releasing ownership while final CI/reviews run."
  "2026-10-20T11:52:27.060Z","harness:codex","SDK authoring follow-up observed during mutation admission: distinguish runtime-schema option identities from extension item-field assignments. The field option currently addresses active extension registrations only; a runtime-schema key such as escape_class is refused there and must use its direct schema option through the generic run route. New PmClient create/update runtime admission preserves that generic schema path. Audit convenience-method documentation and consider a typed shared custom-field transport rather than implying field covers both registries. Reuse this public-surface consistency owner; no duplicate item or claim is created."
  "2026-10-20T21:21:58.729Z","harness:codex","Additional runtime-schema UX follow-up: close --escape-class currently reports option_scope=declared_nowhere and says the spelling exists on no command path, but create/update help exposes the exact Issue schema option --escape-class (and update accepts the defect metadata). The immediate correct workflow is update the schema fields, then use close with resolution/expected/actual. The closed lexicon-scope predecessor pm-in23qu delivered core declared/elsewhere/nowhere classification; this new counterexample concerns dynamic type-schema flags omitted from that membership census. Reuse this existing public-surface/schema-option owner and its earlier escape_class namespace note; no duplicate item or claim. Future acceptance: runtime contracts and unknown-option recovery include schema-provided flags with their accepting paths/type conditions, and a negative control contrasts this real elsewhere spelling with a truly nonexistent flag. No flag alias or new command is requested."
  "2026-10-20T21:35:40.123Z","harness:codex","PR #1526 review follow-up: added the five missing function descriptions identified by CodeRabbit's diff-scoped 68.75% docstring warning (four new advisory fixture helpers and the touched assurance adoption dispatcher). Build, repository docstring quality, targeted ESLint and the focused linked suite pass. The implementation head 206adc231 passed every required free GitHub check with no pending or missing publishers, and both actionable review threads are fixed/resolved. This documentation slice is complete; the broader public-surface programme and newly recorded runtime-schema recovery enhancement remain open. Returning this owner to open and releasing its claim before final current-head CI and full re-review."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-15T19:41:35.150Z",maintainer-agent,"Companion-repo SDK doc duplication evidence (pass #90, 2026-07-15): unbraind/pm-cli-companion hosts docs/TYPESCRIPT_SDK.md — a full parallel \"TypeScript SDK Guide ... covers every capability type with working examples\" — alongside website-server/views/sdk.ejs, while the canonical in-repo doc is docs/SDK.md (2265 lines). Two hand-maintained full SDK guides in two repos = drift by construction; fold into this item's \"website/plugin copy still to check\" ledger. Fix direction at execution: generate the companion page from the canonical doc (or reduce it to a pointer + quickstart), never hand-sync. In-repo SDK docs trio (SDK.md / SDK_CUSTOMIZATION_PRIMITIVES.md / SDK_PRIMITIVE_INVENTORY.md) verified deliberately partitioned with distinct purposes and tracked owners — no in-repo duplication defect."
  "2026-09-08T06:04:02.626Z","harness:codex","Capability adoption/coverage ledger: adopt progressive context/contracts/help, all-status receipts, bounded cursor events, live item/history reads, typed graph analysis, strict duplicate discovery, atomic mutation batches, artifact links, linked sandbox tests, semantic reindex and published consumer verification. Cover destructive recovery, imports, schema changes, remote authorization, MCP subscriptions/apps/skills and fault paths through their existing isolated test contracts rather than inventing production state to exercise them. Waive artificial reminders/meetings/roles, synthetic production training episodes and speculative destructive compaction for this planning pass. Each waiver is scope-specific, not a claim that the feature was tested here. All four skills route to generated complete capabilities; detailed procedures remain progressive references."
  "2026-09-08T06:23:16.934Z","harness:codex","Skill/documentation delivery evidence 2026-09-08: all four PM skills route to the generated complete CLI/SDK/MCP capability map and retain progressive disclosure. The planning reference explains complete-population receipts, history versus event collection, typed edge evidence, algorithm ownership and truthful closeout. Developer guidance uses automatic identity, structured close-event evidence and per-stream history verification; SDK package export examples and multi-agent merge instructions were corrected. New portfolio and test-isolation references are linked and pass the docs/skills gate. Source artifact links cover the complete tracked non-PM tree. Remaining broad programme scope includes external website/plugin consistency and future contract-driven drift, so retain the programme as open."
